---
import Machine from "../components/Machine.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="llmcpu"
  description="A language model wired up as the control unit of a tiny computer, running real binaries and anything else you feed it, in your browser."
>
  <div class="intro">
    <h1>A language model, pretending to be a CPU</h1>
    <p>
      The bytes of a real program sit in memory. A small language model, running on your graphics card, has to read them
      four at a time, work out what each one means, and carry it out with a handful of tools. Beside it, an ordinary
      silicon processor runs the same bytes so you can see where the model gets it wrong. Then feed it something that
      was never a program at all, and watch it carry on anyway.
    </p>
  </div>
  <Machine />
</Base>

<style>
  .intro {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    max-width: var(--prose-width);
    margin-block-end: var(--space-5);
  }

  .intro p {
    font-size: var(--step1);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
</style>
